      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>SJC</at:authority-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Shaojiang Chinese is a Min Chinese language centered on Western Nanping in Northwest Fujian. The classification of Shao–Jiang is disputed. It is frequently classified as a variety of Northern Min, but sometimes it is excluded from Min and classified as Gan Chinese instead. But it is mutually intelligible with neither other Northern Min nor other Gan.</skos:definition>
