      <skos:altLabel xml:lang="en">Jiwarli</skos:altLabel>
      <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#XML_LNG">dze</skos:notation>
      <skos:notation rdf:datatype="http://publications.europa.eu/ontology/euvoc#ISO_639_3">dze</skos:notation>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Djiwarli</skos:prefLabel>
      <dc:identifier>DZE</dc:identifier>
      <atold:op-code>DZE</atold:op-code>
      <at:op-code>DZE</at:op-code>
      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>DZE</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>dze</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Djiwarli, also known as Jiwarli, is a Mantharta language spoken in the Pilbara region of Western Australia. It is closely related to Thiin (iin). Together with other Mantharta languages it belongs to the Pama–Nyungan language family, the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
