      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="cs">romština</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="lt">romų kalba</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="mt">Zingaru</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="uk">циганська мова</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="ru">цыга́нский</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="sl">romščina</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="lv">čigānu valoda</skos:prefLabel>
      <dc:identifier>ROM</dc:identifier>
      <atold:op-code>ROM</atold:op-code>
      <at:op-code>ROM</at:op-code>
      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>ROM</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>rom</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>PUB</dc:source>
            <at:affected-table>PUB_LNGISO</at:affected-table>
            <at:legacy-code>0B</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>PUB</dc:source>
            <at:affected-table>PUB_LANG</at:affected-table>
            <at:legacy-code>0B</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-2t</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>rom</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-2b</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>rom</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Romani (also Romany or Gypsy) is a Balkanised neo-Indo-European language belonging to the Indo-Aryan branch. It is spoken principally in Europe by Romani people.The alphabets used in the different varieties of the Romany generally correspond to those countries where the corresponding Roma communities live. The alphabets of use are the Latin, the Cyrillic, the Arabic and the Greek alphabets.</skos:definition>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Le romani est une langue néo-indo-européenne balkanisée appartenant à la branche indo-aryenne. Il est parlé principalement en Europe par les Roms.Les alphabets utilisés dans les différentes variantes du romani correspondent généralement à ceux des pays où vivent les communautés roms concernées. Les alphabets utilisés sont le latin, le cyrillique, l’arabe et le grec.</skos:definition>
      <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">Documentation for ISO 639 identifier ‘ROM’: The individual languages within this macrolanguage are: Balkan Romani rmn, Baltic Romani rml, Carpathian Romani rmc, Finnish Kalo rmf, Sinte Romani rmo, Vlax Romani rmy, Welsh Romani rmw.</skos:changeNote>
      <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">0B</skos:changeNote>
   </skos:Concept>
