      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Kwak [kwq] appeared as Nkwak in the 1992 Index of Nigerian Languages (Crozier and Blench 1992), but was withdrawn from the 3rd edition (Blench 1999) since it had been discovered as a place in in the Hyam area13. In E17, Kwak is listed as a dialect of Yamba [yam].</skos:scopeNote>
