      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Romam belongs to the Bahnaric primary branch of the Austroasiatic language family. It is spoken in the Central Highlands of Vietnam. Together with its closest relative, Kachok, Romam forms the Lamamic group, though the two languages are quite distinct.</skos:definition>
