      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Kulon-Pazeh subgroup was proposed in Blust (1999); however, Kulon and Pazeh-Kaxabu are two different languages. Thus, Kulon-Pazeh [uun] split into Kulon [uon] and Pazeh [pzh]</skos:scopeNote>
