         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Central Atlas Tamazight is a Berber language of the Afroasiatic language family spoken in the Atlas Mountains of Central Morocco as well as by smaller emigrant communities in France and elsewhere. It is one of the most-spoken Berber languages. It is officially written in the Tifinagh script for instruction in Moroccan schools while descriptive linguistic literature commonly uses the Latin alphabet, and the Arabic alphabet has also been used.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
