         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Shabak is an Indo-Iranian language and belongs to the subgroup Zaza-Gorani of the Northwestern Iranian languages. The Shabaki language is spoken by the Shabak people in the Mosul region of northern Iraq. It is a subdialect of the Kurdish dialect Gorani alongside Hewrami, Sarli, and Bajalan. It also been influenced by Arabic, Turkish and Persian language.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
