            <at:legacy-code>jay</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Yan-nhangu, also known as Nhangu, is a Pama-Nyungan language within the Yolngu sub-branch. It is spoken by the Yan-nhangu people in Australia's Northern Territory. The Pama–Nyungan languages are the most widespread family of Australian Aboriginal languages, comprising over 300 of the approximately 400 Aboriginal languages of Australia.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
