      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">"Chimakum" is just an alternate spelling for Chemakum, which is the more common
spelling in the linguistic literature. However, since it has been listed with this spelling in the Ethnologue, it is probably appropriate to include this alternate spelling in the standard [xch].</skos:scopeNote>
      <at:end.use>2010-01-18</at:end.use>
