      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Kirmanjki (Kirmanckî) or Northern Zaza is an Indo-Iranian language spoken primarily in eastern Turkey. The language is a part of the Zaza–Gorani language group of the northwestern group of the Iranian branch.</skos:definition>
