      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>YNB</at:authority-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Yamben, also spelled Yaben, is a Trans–New Guinea language of Madang Province, Papua New Guinea. It was first documented by Andrew Pick in the 2010s and classified by Pick (2019) as a probable primary branch of Madang, though its precise classification is still pending further research.</skos:definition>
