      <at:authority-code>YRI</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>yri</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">his name does not appear in any of the main published sources. Hammarstrom (2015) comes to the same conclusion, indicating that the location given for Yarí in Colombia is Carijona [cbd] territory. For these reasons this language probably does not exist and the code should be retired.</skos:scopeNote>
      <at:end.use>2016-01-15</at:end.use>
   </skos:Concept>
