      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">Manually added collection language</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Sign languages are languages which mainly use signs made with the hands, the arms or the body and facial expressions. Sign languages have been developed for communities of deaf people but are also used by people with speaking disability.</skos:definition>
