      <atold:op-code>SMD</atold:op-code>
      <at:op-code>SMD</at:op-code>
      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>SMD</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>smd</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">There is no evidence that Sama [smd] exists as a distinct speech variety used by a community with a unique ethnolinguistic identity. It is a regional dialect of Kimbundu [kmb], spoken in the municipality of Quissama (spelling varies) in northwestern Angola's Luanda Province.</skos:scopeNote>
      <at:end.use>2022-01-20</at:end.use>
