         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Moi-Wadea (Moi, Maniwo, Dao) and Auye (Auwje) are the two varieties of a Papuan language group spoken in the Paniai lakes region of the Indonesian province of Central Papua. Both belong to the Nuclear Trans New Guinea language family.</skos:definition>
