      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Dyarim is an Afro-Asiatic language spoken in Nigeria. It belongs to the endangered Western Chadic sub-branch whose speakers are shifting to Hausa. One of its closest relatives is the Zeemic language group.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
