      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">As Hammerstrom notes, "It has been known for a century that the Sru were a fraction of the Ukit [umi] who happened to end up at Sru, and indeed, "every word . . . " in the wordlist of Bailey (1901) was understood by the Ukit [umi] "as belonging to their own language".</skos:scopeNote>
