      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>TVI</at:authority-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Tulai is an Afro-Asiatic language spoken in Nigeria. It belongs to the endangered Western Chadic sub-branch whose speakers are shifting to Hausa. Together with Cha'ari and Zeem, it forms the Nuclear Zeemic group.</skos:definition>
