      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>btl</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Shukla (1986:22) says that Bhatola does not exist. This language does not appear in the listing of Scheduled Tribes (Singh 1997). The Ethnologue has no information on the language, reporting that it is unclassified. Hammarstrom (2015) agrees with the assessment that the language does not exist.</skos:scopeNote>
      <at:end.use>2016-01-15</at:end.use>
