      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Ekai Chin, also known as Läoktü Chin, is a Tibeto-Burman language falling under the Kuki-Chin sub-branch of the Sino-Tibetan language family. The Ekai are the largest group along Dalet Stream in northern Ann Township, Rakhine State, Myanmar. Compared to Sinitic languages, Kuki-Chin languages are tonal but less so, and they are less isolating and more morphologically structured. They also tend to display areal features with neighbouring Austro-Asiatic languages.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
