      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Montenegrin</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="uk">чорногорська мова</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="ru">черногорский язык</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="is">svartfellska</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Montenegrinisch</skos:prefLabel>
      <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="sr">црногорски језик</skos:prefLabel>
      <dc:identifier>0E0</dc:identifier>
      <atold:op-code>0E0</atold:op-code>
      <at:op-code>0E0</at:op-code>
      <at:start.use>2006-06-03</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>0E0</at:authority-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">ISO 639-2 and 639-3 codes "cnr" were assigned to Montenegrin on 8.12.2017.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This authority code is retired as according to RFC 5646 and iana subtag-registry the first part of the code must not have decimals.</skos:historyNote>
      <at:end.use>2017-12-07</at:end.use>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Montenegrin is the standardised variety of the Serbo-Croatian used by Montenegrins. It is based on the Shtokavian dialect of Serbo-Croatian.Montenegrin uses more the Latin alphabet than the Cyrillic. In both alphabets there are two additional letters.</skos:definition>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="fr">Le monténégrin est la variante normalisée du serbo-croate utilisé par les Monténégrins. Il est basé sur le dialecte chtokavien du serbo-croate.Le monténégrin emploie plus l’alphabet latin que cyrillique. Dans les deux alphabets, il y a deux lettres supplémentaires.</skos:definition>
      <skos:changeNote xml:lang="en">Montenegrin has no ISO-639 language codes.</skos:changeNote>
      <skos:changeNote xml:lang="fr">Le monténégrin n'a pas de codes langue ISO-639.</skos:changeNote>
   </skos:Concept>
