      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>LMM</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>lmm</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">There is no Lamam language in Cambodia. The Ethnologue improperly moved it to Vietnam, but there is already a Romam language in Vietnam. The Romam in Vietnam is confined to one village, numbering between 200-400 people in Le village, Mo Rai commune.</skos:scopeNote>
      <at:end.use>2014-02-03</at:end.use>
   </skos:Concept>
