      <dc:identifier>IKH</dc:identifier>
      <atold:op-code>IKH</atold:op-code>
      <at:op-code>IKH</at:op-code>
      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>IKH</at:authority-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Ikhin-Arokho is an Edoid language spoken in Edo State in Nigeria. Together with Emai-Iuleha-Ora, it forms the Emaic subgroup. Similar to the more well-known Bantu languages, Ikhin-Arokho also features noun class systems, which are a key characteristic used to identify the broader Atlantic–Congo language family, to which Ikhin-Arokho belongs as part of the Volta–Congo primary branch.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
