         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Southeast Tasmanian, or Nuenonne, a name shared with Bruny Island Tasmanian, is an Aboriginal language or pair of languages of Tasmania in the reconstruction of Claire Bowern. It was spoken on the southeastern coast of Tasmania.</skos:definition>
