      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Dokshi is an Afro-Asiatic language spoken in Nigeria. It belongs to the endangered Western Chadic sub-branch whose speakers are shifting to Hausa. Together with the Nuclear Zeemic, it forms the Zeemic group of languages.</skos:definition>
