      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">Pamlico is the name of a tribe (ethnonym) whose members spoke a dialect of Carolina Algonquian
[crr]. Pamlico is sometimes used as an alternate name for Carolina Algonquian (Mithun 1999: 327, 333).</skos:scopeNote>
