      <at:authority-code>ZLM</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>zlm</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Malay is a major language of the Austronesian family. Malay (zlm) refers to local Malay dialects that differ substantially from Standard Malay. Therefore Malay (zlm) is a non-standard dialect cluster spoken in Malesia and Sumatra. Glottolog defines zlm as a Central Malay dialect cluster, covering such dialects as Riau Malay, Johor Malay, Melaka Malay and Kuala Lumpur Malay.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
