      <dc:identifier>IBI</dc:identifier>
      <atold:op-code>IBI</atold:op-code>
      <at:op-code>IBI</at:op-code>
      <at:start.use>1950-05-09</at:start.use>
      <at:authority-code>IBI</at:authority-code>
      <at:op-mapped-code>
         <at:MappedCode>
            <dc:source>iso-639-3</dc:source>
            <at:legacy-code>ibi</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The change I am proposing is that Ibilo [ibi] be changed from being a language within [Edo-Esan-Ora, North Central, Edoid, Benue-Congo, Volta-Congo, Atlantic-Congo, Niger-Congo], and be moved to being a dialect of Okpamheri [opa], located within the Northwestern Edoid branch.</skos:scopeNote>
      <at:end.use>2012-02-03</at:end.use>
   </skos:Concept>
