      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Zeem is an Afro-Asiatic language spoken in Nigeria. It belongs to the endangered Western Chadic sub-branch whose speakers are shifting to Hausa. Together with Tulai and Cha'ari, it forms the Nuclear Zeemic group.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
