      <skos:historyNote xml:lang="en">This code is deprecated in ISO 639-3. It is no longer in active use, but still has the meaning assigned to it when it was established in the Standard.</skos:historyNote>
      <skos:scopeNote xml:lang="en">The Ditidaht language is recognized as an individual language by the First Peoples' Heritage, Language and Culture Council. Thus, Nootka [noo] split into Ditidaht [dtd] and Nuu-chah-nulth [nuk].</skos:scopeNote>
