      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Bajelani is an Indo-Iranian language and considered a dialect of Gorani of the Northwestern Iranian language group with about 59 000 speakers, predominately around Mosul, near Khanaqin and near the Khosar valley.</skos:definition>
