      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Brao (Brou, Palaw, Preou) is a Mon–Khmer language spoken in and around the town of Taveng in Ratanakiri Province, Cambodia. Brao falls under the Bahnaric sub-branch of the Austroasiatic language family.</skos:definition>
