            <at:legacy-code>gdh</at:legacy-code>
         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Gajirrabeng is an Aboriginal Australian language spoken by Gajirrawoong people, most of whom now live in the Northern Territory in north-eastern Western Australia. It has been classified as one of two Mirriwongic languages, the other being Miriwoong. More recent work has established it as a member of the Jarrakan group.</skos:definition>
   </skos:Concept>
