      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Minnan or Southern Min is a group of linguistically similar and historically related Chinese languages that form a branch of Min Chinese spoken in Fujian, most of Taiwan, Eastern Guangdong, Hainan and Southern Zhejiang.</skos:definition>
      <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/ZHO"/>
