         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Southern Kurdish (Pehlewani) is a Kurdish dialect predominantly spoken in western Iran and eastern Iraq. Native speakers use various different alphabets to write Southern Kurdish, the most common ones are extensions of the standard Kurdish alphabets (Latin or Perso-Arabic script). This language is part of the Kurdish group within the northwestern branch of the Indo-Iranian languages.</skos:definition>
      <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/KUR"/>
   </skos:Concept>
