      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Central Kurdish (Sorani) is a Kurdish dialect spoken in Iraq, mainly in Iraqi Kurdistan, as well as the Kurdistan Province of western Iran. The language is written in an adapted form of the Kurdo-Arabic alphabet. The language is part of the Kurdish group within the northwestern branch of the Indo-Iranian languages.</skos:definition>
      <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/KUR"/>
   </skos:Concept>
