      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Jahanka is a Manding language of Guinea-Bissau and Guinea. It is partially intelligible with Mandinka. Manding languages are a sub-branch of Mande languages that are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis.</skos:definition>
      <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/MAN"/>
   </skos:Concept>
