         </at:MappedCode>
      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Bolon is a Manding language of Burkina Faso. There are two dialects, White/Southern and Black/Northern; White Bolon is partially intelligible with Jula. Manding languages are a sub-branch of Mande languages that are part of the hypothetical Niger-Congo language family. However, as the Mande languages lack the noun-class morphology, linguists increasingly treat Mande and Atlantic–Congo as independent language families and reject the Niger-Congo hypothesis.</skos:definition>
      <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/MAN"/>
   </skos:Concept>
