      </at:op-mapped-code>
      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Judeo-Persian refers to both a group of Jewish dialects spoken by the Jews living in Iran and Judeo-Persian texts (written in Hebrew alphabet). As a collective term, Judeo-Persian refers to a number of Judeo-Iranian languages spoken by Jewish communities throughout the formerly extensive Persian Empire. The language is part of the Persian group of the southwestern family of the Indo-Iranian languages.</skos:definition>
      <skos:broader rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/language/FAS"/>
   </skos:Concept>
