      <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Classical Sanskrit is a refined and standardized grammatical form that emerged in the mid-1st millennium BCE and was codified in the most comprehensive of ancient grammars, the Aṣṭādhyāyī ('Eight chapters') of Pāṇini.</skos:definition>
